(Title) Tj
T*
(Optimized Nursing Protocols for Hip Replacement Recovery in Older Patients: Study Design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Older adults undergoing hip replacement face prolonged recovery and functional) Tj
T*
(limitations. Enhanced recovery protocols have shown promise in surgical populations.) Tj
T*
(Methods: This single-blind randomized trial will evaluate a structured nursing protocol) Tj
T*
(designed to optimize recovery following hip arthroplasty in 90 patients aged 60 years or) Tj
T*
(older. Participants will be randomized to receive either an optimized multi-component) Tj
T*
(nursing intervention \(ERAS protocol\) or standard postoperative nursing care. The ERAS) Tj
T*
(protocol comprises enhanced pain management, nutritional optimization, early mobilization,) Tj
T*
(catheter management, temperature regulation, and drainage tube care. Outcomes assessed) Tj
T*
(include pain scores, time to first bowel function, time to ambulation, removal of) Tj
T*
(catheters and drains, hip function scores, independence in activities of daily living,) Tj
T*
(complication rates, hospital length of stay, and patient satisfaction. Assessors) Tj
T*
(evaluating outcomes will remain blinded to group assignment. Data will be collected) Tj
T*
(preoperatively and at multiple postoperative intervals. This study aims to determine) Tj
T*
(whether structured nursing interventions can reduce morbidity and hospitalization duration) Tj
T*
(in older hip replacement patients.) Tj
ET
